{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>למועדה</b> — plene with vav, to tell you that six days of the week one is obligated in tefillin, and there are six festival days on which there is no tefillin, and they are: Pesach, Shavuot, Rosh HaShanah, and Yom HaKippurim, Sukkot — שמ\"ע. פארך חבוש = in gematria: these are tefillin." "<b>מימים ימימה</b> — five times in the Masorah here. And the others: מימים ימימה תלכנה וגו' regarding the daughter of Jephthah. חג לה' בשילה מימים ימימה. ועלה האיש ההוא מעירו מימים ימימה regarding Elkanah. והעלתה לו מימים ימימה regarding Samuel. And this is what they expounded: מימים and not all days, to exclude Sabbaths and festivals — and that is why ימימה is written regarding חג ה' and similarly regarding Elkanah and Samuel, who would go up for the pilgrimage festival; and similarly מימים ימימה written regarding the daughter of Jephthah, for women too are exempt from tefillin."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "שמ\"ע appears to be a notarikon for the six festival days listed; the expansion is not provided in the text. פארך חבוש (Song 4:4, 'your braided locks') = 601; אלו תפילין = 601.", 1 "The phrase 'חג לה\" בשילה מימים ימימה' does not correspond to any biblical verse verbatim; it appears to be a paraphrastic conflation of Judges 21:19 and the Jephthah narrative context, rendered here as it stands in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:48.246662345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}